  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">One Health Partnerships (Asia-Pacific)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment consists of four agreements with key partners building regional One Health capacity: 
1. The Australia-World Organisation for Animal Health (WOAH) One Health Partnership - building capacity of national animal health services across the region; 
2. The Australia- Food and Agriculture Organisation (FAO) One Health Partnership - building regional veterinary field epidemiology training capacity and networks, plus mitigating the risks of zoonotic disease spillover in wildlife wet markets in Sulawesi, Indonesia and building animal husbandry and production capacity in the Pacific; 
3. The Pacific Paraveterinary Partnerships Project, by the Department of Agriculture, Fisheries and Forestry (DAFF) - building practical training aspects of paraveterinary training across the Pacific, PNG and Timor-Leste; and 
4. Regional One Health Partnerships, by the Australian Centre for International Agriculture Research (ACIAR) - conducting One Health research projects across the region.</narrative>
  </description>
